{
  "ruling": "On the facts recorded, AuditRequirement is modelled as a product of two fields: `kind : String` and `threshold : Nat`. That is the whole of the model the record discloses, and the ruling extends no further: it fixes the shape and the field types, and nothing about permitted values, invariants on `threshold`, or the meaning of any particular `kind`.",
  "reasoning": "The question asks how a type is modelled and the facts supply exactly one thing — a two-field record, `kind:String,threshold:Nat`. The weakest reading the facts support is that the recorded fields and their types are the model; anything stronger (that `kind` is drawn from a closed enumeration, that `threshold` is bounded, that the fields are ordered or exhaustive of some wider schema) would be read into a record that does not contain it, which is making law rather than applying it (Law s.5). I therefore take the structural reading and decline the wider question of what values these fields may lawfully hold, and of whether `String` is the right carrier for `kind` — that question is not on this record and would need facts about the admissible kinds before a bench could sit on it. I note but do not act on Law s.7: no actor is named here, and none is needed, because this is a question of how a thing is modelled and not a question of who may perform an act — a ruling declaring a type's shape permits no one to do anything, so there is no missing actor for a reader to supply. Nothing in the law in force bears on the choice of representation, and no prior ruling was cited or found on this key, so the matter is decided at first instance and stands until superseded (Law s.1, s.3).",
  "lawApplied": [
    "The law of this court, II.5 (Decide the question asked; prefer the weakest reading the facts support; name the choice taken; decline the wider question)",
    "The law of this court, I.1 (A question decided is not decided again — no standing ruling on this key, so the bench sits)",
    "The law of this court, I.3 (Nothing is deleted; this ruling stands until superseded)",
    "The law of this court, III.7 (The actor must be stated — considered and held inapplicable to a question of modelling, which authorises no act)"
  ]
}
